{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013274-vampire-lite","id":1013274,"title":"\"Vampire Lite\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-06T11:05:47-08:00","id":1013274,"title":"\"Vampire Lite\"","content":"So someone referred to Vampire: The Requiem as &quot;Vampire Lite.&quot;<br /> <br /> I found this odd given that I have read both V:TR editions and supplements, and I didn't find this &quot;lite&quot; at all. If I did, I wouldn't want to play it more if it were truly &quot;lite&quot; but is there anything in the game that could possibly be interpreted this way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T11:19:11-08:00","id":1013280,"title":"","content":"I think there's been a shift in players and perception. I don't believe it's about the game but perhaps about the current kinds of people approaching the game.<br /> <br /> Just based on what I've seen on other forums talking about it and this one, it does seem like there's more people who want to play vampire but not play a monster. There's people who want to play a vampire as a cool action hero or martyrish tragic hero. And an increased pushback against more sinister options for characters.<br /> <br /> That said, it could just be considered 'Vampire Lite' because it doesn't come with a monolithic fictional background behind it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T11:20:39-08:00","id":1013282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013274-vampire-lite?p=1013280#post1013280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's been a shift in players and perception. I don't believe it's about the game but perhaps about the current kinds of people approaching the game.<br /> <br /> Just based on what I've seen on other forums talking about it and this one, it does seem like there's more people who want to play vampire but not play a monster. There's people who want to play a vampire as a cool action hero or martyrish tragic hero. And an increased pushback against more sinister options for characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>People like this have always been playing, but yeah, I can see there being more than before.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013274-vampire-lite?p=1013280#post1013280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, it could just be considered 'Vampire Lite' because it doesn't come with a monolithic fictional background behind it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn't considered this. Requiem is <i>definitely</i> lite in this regard. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T11:24:08-08:00","id":1013286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013274-vampire-lite?p=1013282#post1013282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People like this have always been playing, but yeah, I can see there being more than before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, I should have pointed out that I wasn't part of the community back in the 'old days' and I'm sure that it was similar then, as such things are never as nice as people remember.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T11:44:06-08:00","id":1013296,"title":"","content":"Sounds like something a salty Masquerade fan might say about Requiem. The Requiem 1e core probably looked like Masquerade Lite at the time it came out. Masquerade had 13 main Clans and countless Bloodlines compared to Requiem's 5 of each at the time of its initial releasee. Masquerade had 10 years of metaplot while Requiem was brand new and intentionally metaplot-free, which probably made it look like it had no plot depth to people who were used to the extensive plot of Masquerade. In 1st Edition, White Wolf was very conservative with vampires' powers, making Requiem vampires seem weak in comparison to Masquerade vampires.<br /> <br /> And it didn't help that Requiem kept flirting with concepts from Masquerade, but changing them. Three of the Clans shared names with Masquerade Clans, but with different weaknesses and Discipline spreads. Three of the Bloodlines were named after Masquerade Clans but were much narrower in focus. The city power structure that was presented as the default was almost identical to Camarilla-run cities, and the book actually said that most cities are run basically the same, but different Covenants might use different titles for effectively the same positions, which made it look like despite there being five Covenants compared to Masquerade's three Sects (give or take a Sect, depending on how you count), they were all basically just different palette swaps of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> All this on top of the fact that, at the time, Masquerade was over. Gehenna had happened, the world had ended, and White Wolf was moving on. No more new books were going to be made for the &quot;old&quot; World of Darkness, in favor of supporting this &quot;new&quot; one. the Camarilla Fan Club was switching its LARP over to Requiem. If you loved Masquerade and were hesitant about this new Requiem, you'd understandably be bitter that this seemingly watered-down, less nuanced vampire game was replacing the game you'd spent the last decade enjoying. And so, you might try to convince your friends not to play this new &quot;Vampire Lite&quot;, and to stick with Masquerade instead. Don't support this new direction White Wolf is taking and maybe they'll see the error of their ways.<br /> <br /> Of course, as we've seen, they did eventually bring the classic World of Darkness back, and at present it's got more supplement support than Chronicles of Darkness. Meanwhile, Chronicles has had 10+ years to develop, and has really come into its own identity as a setting completely independent of World of Darkness, despite a few artifacts like Clan names that are too ingrained change at this point. Requiem has made a lot of changes that address many of the concerns people had about the 1st edition core book. To call Requiem &quot;Masquerade Lite&quot; today just shows that a person is still letting that initial perception of Requiem from reading that first core book (or worse, maybe even from second or third hand information about that first core book) shape their concept of Requiem today.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-06-2016, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T11:50:39-08:00","id":1013298,"title":"","content":"Oh, or it might be folks who think Requiem is too &quot;PC&quot;. I've seen a lot of arguments from Masquerade fans that the fact that the Clans are based on offensive stereotypes is part of what makes the World of Darkness &quot;dark&quot; or &quot;punk&quot;, or &quot;realistic&quot;, and that if you want a &quot;sanitized&quot; vampire game you should go play Requiem (which is implied to be an inferior game for it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-06-2016, 02:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T12:45:58-08:00","id":1013336,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: Vampire Lite - </b><br /> <br /> Maybe this is completely anecdotal, but I have been playing in the World of Darkness since Vampire the Masquerade 1st edition came out and I picked up a copy from the local gaming store. I still have a collection of all the editions and a good chunk of the supplements going back over 20 years (yes, I'm old) . And I can say with all honesty that I didn't get to run the Vampire game that the first edition book promised until Requiem. Vampire games in Masquerade often felt like action movies (trenchcoats and silver katanas galore!) and many players who crossed my table approached it like a darker super hero setting. I love so much of what Masquerade offers - but I honestly think Requiem does many of the core themes better. The exploration of the descent into monstrosity seems more focused and more central in Requiem, and much deeper than &quot;How many mortals did your antitribu brutalize this week&quot;. <br /> IMHO, those that dismissed Requiem early on did themselves a disservice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T13:03:01-08:00","id":1013342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013274-vampire-lite?p=1013298#post1013298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, or it might be folks who think Requiem is too &quot;PC&quot;. I've seen a lot of arguments from Masquerade fans that the fact that the Clans are based on offensive stereotypes is part of what makes the World of Darkness &quot;dark&quot; or &quot;punk&quot;, or &quot;realistic&quot;, and that if you want a &quot;sanitized&quot; vampire game you should go play Requiem (which is implied to be an inferior game for it).</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone really needs to explain to me how writing big gobs of text about racism makes these books more punk. I do not compute. Have I been going about this all wrong? Did I need to put more KKK werewolves in my writing? Or, like, country-club-racist vampires (they're not, like, <i>racist </i>racist, but you know, it's kinda <i>white </i>over at Elysium, if ya know what I'm saying)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T13:04:02-08:00","id":1013343,"title":"","content":"In my experience Masquerade was treated like superheroes with fangs, and Requiem the more grounded and serious one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8762-waywardpaladin","name":"WaywardPaladin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T13:06:43-08:00","id":1013345,"title":"","content":"Agreed, completely.<br /> <br /> I'm a Vampire fan since the 90s, and I love the promises the 1st core of Masquerade make. But was Requiem whom delivered most of it. I'm still a Masquerade fan, and play it a lot, but that game simply isn't all that some people say it is. And a lot of people deride Requiem without even knowing it, just because of Masquerade. That is sad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T14:49:57-08:00","id":1013396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013274-vampire-lite?p=1013342#post1013342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Someone really needs to explain to me how writing big gobs of text about racism makes these books more punk. I do not compute. Have I been going about this all wrong? Did I need to put more KKK werewolves in my writing? Or, like, country-club-racist vampires (they're not, like, <i>racist </i>racist, but you know, it's kinda <i>white </i>over at Elysium, if ya know what I'm saying)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't quite understand what is meant by punk, but I think that in this context, it involves rebellion against oppression. So such a story requires some sort of oppressors. Usually elders in Masquerade and somewhat less frequently, the First and Second Estates in Requiem. When such antagonists are more egalitarian in many ways than the living I'd say that it starts to feel slightly <i>utopian</i>. (Awakening) Mage society, for all their flaws, arguably is inherently enlightened (having an instant global telecommunications network since probably before the Norse found the Americas is bound develop a culture) so I'd say that it makes a lot of sense there. Whereas there is a rule of thumb popular some fans, including myself, that <i>vampires ruin everything</i>. Such is the World of Darkness isn't it?<br /> <br /> I think that <i>Requiem for Rome </i>especially defies some of these criticisms (including metaplot and clan stereotypes). In a section about slave markets, it actually says that the discomfort that a player may feel raising money to buy a slave their freedom rather than breaking into the market &quot;may be entirely appropriate for a horror game&quot;. To me, these games are about horrors both otherworldly and human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T15:02:51-08:00","id":1013404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013274-vampire-lite?p=1013396#post1013396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <i>vampires ruin everything</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see you've read our brochure!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T16:53:42-08:00","id":1013483,"title":"","content":"&quot;Vampires ruin everything&quot; is my new motto since last week or so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T18:09:09-08:00","id":1013506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013274-vampire-lite?p=1013483#post1013483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Vampires ruin everything&amp;quot; is my new motto since last week or so.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in my signature now so it must be true!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T18:53:00-08:00","id":1013523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013274-vampire-lite?p=1013296#post1013296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like something a salty Masquerade fan might say about Requiem. The Requiem 1e core probably looked like Masquerade Lite at the time it came out. Masquerade had 13 main Clans and countless Bloodlines compared to Requiem's 5 of each at the time of its initial releasee. Masquerade had 10 years of metaplot while Requiem was brand new and intentionally metaplot-free, which probably made it look like it had no plot depth to people who were used to the extensive plot of Masquerade. In 1st Edition, White Wolf was very conservative with vampires' powers, making Requiem vampires seem weak in comparison to Masquerade vampires.<br /> <br /> And it didn't help that Requiem kept flirting with concepts from Masquerade, but changing them. Three of the Clans shared names with Masquerade Clans, but with different weaknesses and Discipline spreads. Three of the Bloodlines were named after Masquerade Clans but were much narrower in focus. The city power structure that was presented as the default was almost identical to Camarilla-run cities, and the book actually said that most cities are run basically the same, but different Covenants might use different titles for effectively the same positions, which made it look like despite there being five Covenants compared to Masquerade's three Sects (give or take a Sect, depending on how you count), they were all basically just different palette swaps of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> All this on top of the fact that, at the time, Masquerade was over. Gehenna had happened, the world had ended, and White Wolf was moving on. No more new books were going to be made for the &quot;old&quot; World of Darkness, in favor of supporting this &quot;new&quot; one. the Camarilla Fan Club was switching its LARP over to Requiem. If you loved Masquerade and were hesitant about this new Requiem, you'd understandably be bitter that this seemingly watered-down, less nuanced vampire game was replacing the game you'd spent the last decade enjoying. And so, you might try to convince your friends not to play this new &quot;Vampire Lite&quot;, and to stick with Masquerade instead. Don't support this new direction White Wolf is taking and maybe they'll see the error of their ways.<br /> <br /> Of course, as we've seen, they did eventually bring the classic World of Darkness back, and at present it's got more supplement support than Chronicles of Darkness. Meanwhile, Chronicles has had 10+ years to develop, and has really come into its own identity as a setting completely independent of World of Darkness, despite a few artifacts like Clan names that are too ingrained change at this point. Requiem has made a lot of changes that address many of the concerns people had about the 1st edition core book. To call Requiem &quot;Masquerade Lite&quot; today just shows that a person is still letting that initial perception of Requiem from reading that first core book (or worse, maybe even from second or third hand information about that first core book) shape their concept of Requiem today.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you nailed it.<br /> <br /> Although I'm pretty sure Gangrel in both games have the same discipline spread? I mean other than Fortitude/Resilience having a different name in each game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T19:00:53-08:00","id":1013525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013274-vampire-lite?p=1013523#post1013523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, you nailed it.<br /> <br /> Although I'm pretty sure Gangrel in both games have the same discipline spread? I mean other than Fortitude/Resilience having a different name in each game.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do, yeah. Just different weaknesses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T20:56:42-08:00","id":1013572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013274-vampire-lite?p=1013282#post1013282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *snip*<br /> <br /> I hadn't considered this. Requiem is <i>definitely</i> lite in this regard. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bBlessedly so.<br /> <br /> \u200bLike many have already said, Requiem is the game that delivers on the promise of &quot;A Beast I Am, Lest a Beast I Become.&quot; Humanity, and the gaining and losing of it, is so central to the game in the 2nd edition, that it's almost an entirely separate game from the 1st edition. If someone hasn't taken the time to familiarize themselves with B&amp;S and was only relying on their impression from 1st edition, I can definitely see that as &quot;Vampire Lite.&quot; <br /> <br /> Funnily enough, that was almost me. It was only after I picked up a copy of the Player's Guide did Requiem become more than &quot;that not-Vampire Vampire game&quot; to me. It started me down the path that ultimately led to Rose's actual play on rpg.net. Once I read that, everything clicked and I *understood.* Then I found out that she was the main developer and I converted completely. I came around and can profess my faith in the one, true Vampire game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1257-kerensky","name":"Kerensky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T22:29:16-08:00","id":1013602,"title":"","content":"I think the main thrust of the &quot;Vampire Lite&quot; complaints is mistaking a different design paradigm the Clans (loose archetypes over detailed histories) for inferiority. Too many diehard Masquerade fans don't seem to realize that Requiem isn't doing things worse than their preferred game, it's doing things entirely differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T00:19:14-08:00","id":1013620,"title":"","content":"From personal experiences the two main groups of players who escribe to the &quot;Vampire Lite&quot; belief for Requiem that I've encountered are either the dismissive types who simply refuse to associate at all with anything from Requiem in favor of Madquerade, or players who are used to...well, let's call it a certain level of power fantasy with their vampire games. The latter also tend to routinely have words like: Celerity, Potence, Vissicitide, Hidden Diablerist, Quietus, Unbondable, Low Generation, and of course Thaumaturgy and Necromancy Paths writen on their Masquerade character sheets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T01:20:28-08:00","id":1013634,"title":"","content":"I like Requiem because it provides enough detail to be interesting, but still gives Storytellers enough room to build their own overarching history and plotlines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T01:27:29-08:00","id":1013640,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't really know what that means either. The most probable option is the Masquerade nostalgia like it's been said. I can understand mourning the metaplot. Games with one can be interesting to play because it gives pointers for events the players might take part in. Without it, you really have to come up with everything yourself, which not everyone is willing to do, although it can be very rewarding if you do it. About the &quot;PC&quot;ness, maybe ? That would be a shame because I feel CoD has been doing an excellent job being dark and depressing without ever being really offensive and falling into numerous edginess pitfalls.<br /> <br /> Is it that the game allows to play a &quot;descent into monstrosity&quot; and is less heroic than Masquerade ? Honestly, I wouldn't know about that. My games have been pretty heroic, with staving off strix invasions from the shadow realm, going to Arcadia to save a friend, fight a vampire civil war to save the city, escape the vampire police and take down it's chief that usurped the Prince that the players never thought they'd miss, and fighting a werewolf, because of course I'm gonna throw a werewolf at you at some point. Most of the time, players are a bit too busy to mope about themselves (and in my last game, they've been incredibly civic, not diablerizing anyone and only intentionally finaldeathing 1 guy, and unintentionally another one). Honestly, I wouldn't have it any other way, and the game's allowed me to do just that every time (with no tweaks the first time, and only a few the second time, where I used 2E), so I don't see where the problem is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T11:07:55-08:00","id":1015739,"title":"","content":"More like Masquerade+, Requiem is superior to it's predecessors in every possible way and don't let a salty Masquerade fanboy tell you otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T11:53:35-08:00","id":1015752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013274-vampire-lite?p=1013298#post1013298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, or it might be folks who think Requiem is too &quot;PC&quot;. I've seen a lot of arguments from Masquerade fans that the fact that the Clans are based on offensive stereotypes is part of what makes the World of Darkness &quot;dark&quot; or &quot;punk&quot;, or &quot;realistic&quot;, and that if you want a &quot;sanitized&quot; vampire game you should go play Requiem (which is implied to be an inferior game for it).</div> </div> </div> </div>I shared this exact opinion though i dont think it makes Requiem a worse game for that. Its more, if the stereotypes and what not by their mere existence really disrupt your enjoyment of the game then there is always Requiem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013274-vampire-lite?p=1013342#post1013342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone really needs to explain to me how writing big gobs of text about racism makes these books more punk. I do not compute. Have I been going about this all wrong? Did I need to put more KKK werewolves in my writing? Or, like, country-club-racist vampires (they're not, like, <i>racist </i>racist, but you know, it's kinda <i>white </i>over at Elysium, if ya know what I'm saying)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is more about how in OWoD contrary to NWoD (1st) human culture affected the supernatural splats because they were for most of their lives people in said cultures background or how certain questionable choices were product of ideas at the time. For example, the fact that the Dreasmpeakers were forcefully made into an Tradition because to old white europeans hermetics from the colonizations period the idea that shamanistics belief were different between then was unthinkable.<br /> <br /> While 1st edition sat on a unconfortable spot in which it seems human culture and nature didnt affected the supernatural societies or way of thinking as they somehow were &quot;beyond that&quot;. The books maybe once in a while mentioned that other cultures might have their variations but never really made a point of exploring them. So you things like everyone buying the &quot;truths&quot; about the setting (atlantis, father wolf) or societal constructs being somewhat accepted globally without much reason for that to happen. <br /> <br /> <br /> As for the Vampire lite label i have heard it in 2 contexts. The first was as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> explained.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013274-vampire-lite?p=1013296#post1013296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Snip for brevity</div> </div> </div> </div>And the second context was describing the type of play that in OWoD was called Vampions or superhero with fangs in which players/dm ignores the themes of personal horror but when Vampions ignore the themes of personal horror for action, Vampire lite ignore the themes of personal horror for exploring the player &quot;magical realm&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T12:37:13-08:00","id":1015782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013274-vampire-lite?p=1015739#post1015739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More like Masquerade+, Requiem is superior to it's predecessors in every possible way and don't let a salty Masquerade fanboy tell you otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<span style=\"color:#ff0000\">That's edition warring and a violation of the Forum Rules. Don't do it again or your posting privileges will be suspended.<br /> <br /> \u200bPeople can feel free to discuss differences between the games without making statements about one or the other being &quot;better&quot;, personal preferences certainly can be stated, but the moment the discussion becomes argumentative the thread will be closed. Any value judgements being made about fans of one game or the other will also lead to the thread being closed.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 12-11-2016, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T13:44:59-08:00","id":1015815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013274-vampire-lite?p=1015782#post1015782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200b<span style=\"color:#ff0000\">That's edition warring and a violation of the Forum Rules. Don't do it again or your posting privileges will be suspended.<br /> <br /> \u200bPeople can feel free to discuss differences between the games without making statements about one or the other being &quot;better&quot;, personal preferences certainly can be stated, but the moment the discussion becomes argumentative the thread will be closed. Any value judgements being made about fans of one game or the other will also lead to the thread being closed.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Can you link me to the Forum Rules so I could make sure not to get any more of these warnings again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T14:15:11-08:00","id":1015840,"title":"","content":"Check the last line of their sig.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T14:29:44-08:00","id":1015848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013274-vampire-lite?p=1015752#post1015752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I shared this exact opinion though i dont think it makes Requiem a worse game for that. Its more, if the stereotypes and what not by their mere existence really disrupt your enjoyment of the game then there is always Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but the implication is usually that the stereotypes and whatnot enhance one's enjoyment of Masquerade. Which, like, whatever floats your boat I guess? But I can't agree with that opinion. Personally, I see it as something to put up with if you want to play Masquerade, understanding that it is a product of its time and you can't really fix the issues with it without making it a different game. Of course, the consensus seems to be that the game you make it is Requiem, and that's generally presented as a bad thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013274-vampire-lite?p=1015752#post1015752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is more about how in OWoD contrary to NWoD (1st) human culture affected the supernatural splats because they were for most of their lives people in said cultures background or how certain questionable choices were product of ideas at the time. For example, the fact that the Dreasmpeakers were forcefully made into an Tradition because to old white europeans hermetics from the colonizations period the idea that shamanistics belief were different between then was unthinkable.<br /> <br /> While 1st edition sat on a unconfortable spot in which it seems human culture and nature didnt affected the supernatural societies or way of thinking as they somehow were &amp;quot;beyond that&amp;quot;. The books maybe once in a while mentioned that other cultures might have their variations but never really made a point of exploring them. So you things like everyone buying the &amp;quot;truths&amp;quot; about the setting (atlantis, father wolf) or societal constructs being somewhat accepted globally without much reason for that to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, the whole &quot;Human culture doesn't impact supernatural groups in CofD&quot; argument has never made sense to me. Just because supernatural groups aren't parodies of human cultural stereotypes doesn't mean they aren't affect by human culture. And claiming that what you call the truths of the setting are universally accepted (or even that there were in 1st Edition) is simply untrue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013274-vampire-lite?p=1015752#post1015752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Vampire lite label i have heard it in 2 contexts. The first was as <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> explained.<br /> <br /> And the second context was describing the type of play that in OWoD was called Vampions or superhero with fangs in which players/dm ignores the themes of personal horror but when Vampions ignore the themes of personal horror for action, Vampire lite ignore the themes of personal horror for exploring the player &amp;quot;magical realm&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. If people want to play Vampire that way, let them have their fun. We don't need to go around shaming other people's preferences with reductionist labels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013274-vampire-lite?p=1015815#post1015815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you link me to the Forum Rules so I could make sure not to get any more of these warnings again?</div> </div> </div> </div>You really shouldn't post in an online community if you haven't read its code of conduct. The link to the rules is right at the top of the home page, so it really shouldn't be hard to find, but <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\">here you go</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T15:59:29-08:00","id":1015879,"title":"","content":"The stereotypes in Masquerade can get to be a bit much: Malkavians were not a very good representation of mental illness, and the independent clans were practically caricatures in their first edition appearance. One thing that I find odd is that people view the original seven clans as having very narrow stereotypes, but in first edition they were actually fairly broad, similar to the Requiem clans, keeping in mind my comment about the Malkavians.<br /> <br /> One of the things I really like about Requiem is that it went for that broad portrayal and <i>stuck with it</i>. The five clans are quite diverse and while each clan represents certain vampiric stereotypes, they aren't narrow (Requiem Nosferatu being a broader archetype than Masquerade's Nosferatu, for example).<br /> <br /> I mean I love both games, but I found myself wanting to house rule Masquerade into Requiem so I am probably much better off running Requiem than coming up with a host of house rules for Masquerade.<br /> <br /> I don't really care how people play Vampire, although it is a bit frustrating when people assume their preferred play should be universal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T16:08:02-08:00","id":1015882,"title":"","content":"I dislike the notions of &quot;improved masquerade is requiem&quot; or &quot;masquerade sans embarassing bits isn't masquerade.&quot; I think there's plenty to make the game fun and distinct with more grandiose stakes and oddly specific character types. You can have illusionists with strange compulsions and curse-prone assassins be staple character types without being racist (which don't really map to the broader-in-concept requiem clans and covenants.) Most the powers and mechanics are perfectly capable of having more elegant and balanced permutations without ceasing to recognizable. (Except Generation, which is unfair in various specific, narrative-vital manners).<br /> <br /> Any sort of change is bound to make some people upset, especially given that there's plenty of dissent about various editions and character types already. It'd still be nice for there be an edition for me for when I'm feeling a bit more &quot;Vampires who throw fireballs&quot; without having to deal with rock-paper-scissors or 4 attack rolls.<br /> <br /> (For the record, I prefer requiem but I don't like one game being used to shut down discussion of the other.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T16:14:00-08:00","id":1015886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013274-vampire-lite?p=1015882#post1015882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dislike the notions of &quot;improved masquerade is requiem&quot; or &quot;masquerade sans embarassing bits isn't masquerade.&quot; I think there's plenty to make the game fun and distinct with more grandiose stakes and oddly specific character types. You can have illusionists with strange compulsions and curse-prone assassins be staple character types without being racist (which don't really map to the broader-in-concept requiem clans and covenants.) Most the powers and mechanics are perfectly capable of having more elegant and balanced permutations without ceasing to recognizable. (Except Generation, which is unfair in various specific, narrative-vital manners).<br /> <br /> Any sort of change is bound to make some people upset, especially given that there's plenty of dissent about various editions and character types already. It'd still be nice for there be an edition for me for when I'm feeling a bit more &quot;Vampires who throw fireballs&quot; without having to deal with rock-paper-scissors or 4 attack rolls.<br /> <br /> (For the record, I prefer requiem but I don't like one game being used to shut down discussion of the other.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well said. To be clear, I was not meaning to say that I think Masquerade would become Requiem if you removed the unfortunate implications. It's just an argument I have seen from some Masquerade fans, and generally the same ones who use terms like &quot;Vampire Lite&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T02:25:29-08:00","id":1016037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013274-vampire-lite?p=1015882#post1015882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dislike the notions of &amp;quot;improved masquerade is requiem&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;masquerade sans embarassing bits isn't masquerade.&amp;quot; I think there's plenty to make the game fun and distinct with more grandiose stakes and oddly specific character types. You can have illusionists with strange compulsions and curse-prone assassins be staple character types without being racist (which don't really map to the broader-in-concept requiem clans and covenants.) Most the powers and mechanics are perfectly capable of having more elegant and balanced permutations without ceasing to recognizable. (Except Generation, which is unfair in various specific, narrative-vital manners).<br /> <br /> Any sort of change is bound to make some people upset, especially given that there's plenty of dissent about various editions and character types already. It'd still be nice for there be an edition for me for when I'm feeling a bit more &amp;quot;Vampires who throw fireballs&amp;quot; without having to deal with rock-paper-scissors or 4 attack rolls.<br /> <br /> (For the record, I prefer requiem but I don't like one game being used to shut down discussion of the other.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, you do make some really good points there. Plus I see what you're saying in regards to Requiem's Clans and Covenants lacking an instantly recognizable archetype or concept that's pimarily universal to all members. (I.E. The abundance of options can seem like a lack of options. For instance, say Ordo Dracul and any number of images will pop up in any given players mind but say Tremere and one universal idea pops up.)<br /> <br /> However, I would still have to disagree with you in regard to the oddly specific character types not being racist in VtM. Or, more accurately that up until at least Revised the character types in Masquerade suffered from Clan being equated to Race rather than Culture. An yes, a lot of this has been addressing in the more recent V20 supplements (and even DA:V20, which was such a pleasant suprise) like Lore of the Clans and Becket's Jyhad Diary. However, despite all the effort that's been made to make the Clans fully fleshed out cultures with regional differences the fact that once you're embrace you'll be a part of that Clan forever will always reinforce the idea of Race over Cutlure. Even if it's just on a subconscious level. This is why stereotyping the Clans is so easy in Masquerade, and why it's so dangerous since the stereotyping will also be equated with Race over Culture.<br /> <br /> To bring this full circle I think this is exactly why Requiem's Clans are based upon the vampire's condition so heavily over any given culture, while the Covenants are pure culture without any association to any given Clan. That way, despite what Clan you were Embraced into you'd be free to choose whatever culture or ideology that best fit your character. Like mentioned above this is also probably one of the reasons for the Vampire-Lite misconception, since Masquerade players used to the Clan's culture wouldn't find any at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T08:35:07-08:00","id":1016114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013274-vampire-lite?p=1016037#post1016037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> However, I would still have to disagree with you in regard to the oddly specific character types not being racist in VtM. Or, more accurately that up until at least Revised the character types in Masquerade suffered from Clan being equated to Race rather than Culture. An yes, a lot of this has been addressing in the more recent V20 supplements (and even DA:V20, which was such a pleasant suprise) like Lore of the Clans and Becket's Jyhad Diary. However, despite all the effort that's been made to make the Clans fully fleshed out cultures with regional differences the fact that once you're embrace you'll be a part of that Clan forever will always reinforce the idea of Race over Cutlure. Even if it's just on a subconscious level. This is why stereotyping the Clans is so easy in Masquerade, and why it's so dangerous since the stereotyping will also be equated with Race over Culture.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm arguing less a case that they &quot;aren't&quot; racist so much as they &quot;don't have to be&quot; racist while still being able to retain a core identity. OWOD does repeatedly suffer from straddling the line between inherent nature and cultural imperatives.The examples I (quite deliberately) chose, however, are racist because they draw an equivalence between real world stereotypes and real world ethnicities . Designing an oppressively dominate culture for a clan isn't actually being racist in a real world sense. (Though a case could be argued that kind of thinking is at least related to racist attitudes.) The Tremere for example rarely come up when discussing this issue despite having a <b>very</b> specific society entwined with it.<br /> <br /> I also chose to describe those examples in terms that don't actually tie a specific culture. The illusion+compulsion combination can conceivable be meaningfully applied to anyone from anywhere without relying on a clan history. &quot;Assassin&quot; might be a bit more culturally charged term, but stealth and murder are concepts found all over the world and a that's what a particular clan's innate abilities focus on. I think you can dial back on the cultural aspect without sacrificing these flavors. I'm not saying that's what has happened, or is going to happen, but that it <b>can</b> happen. (And even in this case, the concepts are too narrow to fit requiem's clan paradigm.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T13:47:16-08:00","id":1016223,"title":"","content":"Ok, I see what you're saying now <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"526\" data-vbnamecard=\"526\">schizoPOP</a>. In that case we are in agreement, and might I add you summed up my own fears quite nicely and a lot more matter of factly than my previous post. However, you brought up one last topic I'd like to discuss in regards to Masquerade's Clans. And that's the Eugenics undertone.<br /> <br /> Because, it's funny you mentioned the Tremere as an example because unlike the obvious racial &amp; cultural stereotypes Clan Tremere is by far the most subtle and sinister culprit of pushing a eugenic subtext even if unintentionally. And that, of course, is because Clan Tremere represents Academia in the Masquerade setting. They're a race..erh, I mean Clan of occultists and scholars who are known for their intellect, have rigid criteria for new members, indoctrinate potential new members for years about the benefits of completing their harsh ciriculum and the temporal rewards it'll bring alongside the intellectual, enslave new members into debt to their mentors and superiors, don't share esoteric secrets outside of the raClan...the Clan unless payed heavily for them, and upon reaching mastery after decades of hardships and peer pressure they subject the next members through the same bullshit with a smug sense of entitlement and superiority...oh, and they also can do literal magic and are the only raceeaaaClanClan qualified to do literal magic. (Yes, I know. It's not a good joke, but it's supposed to illustrate how sinister the Tremere as a concept is once it interacts with the patern recognition part of your brain.)<br /> <br /> And yes, a looooooooot has been done to remedy this over the years. The Tremere, like all of the Clans, have evolved into an organization of Kindred who share common powers and heritage rather than racial or social stereotype. However, the nature of Clan itself hasn't changed. And that's where the Eugenic subtext comes from. Because the Tremere would work just fine as is if they were just an organization, because that's how Academia is in real life. The fact that you're made into a Tremere, and once made cannot be anything else other than a Tremere, and then have cultural norms thrust upon you irrevocably ties Clan to race. And I feel that's such a waste because so much more could be done in it's place. And luckily, I hope anyways, a good amount of people realize this.<br /> <br /> Because like you said, you can dial back the cultural aspects without sacrificing the Flavors the Clans bring to the table. I completely agree with you in this regards, and feel the easiest solution is to take a leaf from Requiem and have the Masquerade Clans represent a person's physical condition rather than be equated with culture or race. That way, the Cursed Assassin is what she is not because of the society she was Embraced into, but rather because her curse makes her the ideal killing machine. And where or not she chooses to use those talents or not, she'll always have that potential because of the curse. <br /> <br /> [Course Correction: Well, that turned into a rant that I sorta needed to have. To add something meaningful to the Vampire Lite discussion, my biggest fear is that Masquerade players who escribe to the Vampire Lite belief for Requiem mistake the Eugenist undertones of the Clans for depth and substance, and see's their absense in Requiem as a lack of depth and substance. This fear is greatly dissuaded with discussions like the above, and I'm relieved that my own personal experiences with Masquerade aren't the default but rather just really unlucky occurrences. Thank you.]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T13:59:04-08:00","id":1016229,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a> So I didn't see you explain the &quot;eugenicist undertones&quot; in your post. I mean you said it was there, but that seems to be it. Not trying to pick a fight. I am intrigued by this statement and want to know more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T14:22:42-08:00","id":1016239,"title":"","content":"I think you guys are spending too much time thinking about race which leads to reading too deep into something that's not really there. According to modern pop culture: anything and everything is racist, which opens a new question of whether the current subject du jour is <i>actually</i> racist or just &quot;racist&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 12-12-2016, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T14:28:29-08:00","id":1016245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013274-vampire-lite?p=1016239#post1016239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you guys are spending too much time thinking about race which leads to reading too deep into something that's not really there. According to modern pop culture: anything and everything is racist, which opens a new question of whether the current subject du jour is <i>actually</i> racist or just &quot;racist&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not pop culture. Pop culture itself is often racist (not necessarily &quot;always&quot; but certainly &quot;often&quot;).<br /> <br /> IMO, we could do with more critical thinking about race.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T14:29:45-08:00","id":1016248,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a>, good to hear we're on the same page.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T15:45:12-08:00","id":1016284,"title":"","content":"There is a difference between being politically incorrect and pointlessly being insulting.<br /> <br /> Requiem can very politically incorrect, look at stuff like the Wet Dream devotion, vitae addiction, Majesty, Domination, Lashing out, the twisted gory paradories of religions and other beliefs.<br /> <br /> Reqieum doesn't need 2 dimesional stereotypes to be politically incorrect.<br /> <br /> Its fill with sick fucked up people doing sick fucked up things.<br /> <br /> And in someways if Mascarade is about over against oppression, then Reqiuem is the far more realistic depiction of the battle to see who does the oppressing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T16:56:51-08:00","id":1016319,"title":"","content":"When I was getting into this stuff in the 90s, the original World of Darkness attracted a lot of criticism for being &quot;politically correct.&quot; Goalposts shift.<br /> <br /> As it is, <i>Vampire </i>is not particularly polite, nor is it about people who do things correctly. It's about a glorious and unending cavalcade of big mistakes, made for both the best and worst of reasons. We should all be able to see ourselves making those mistakes... and so, <i>Vampire</i> includes diverse characters and viewpoints, in the hope that everyone can get in on the fun of feeling their lives going wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 12-12-2016, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T17:00:06-08:00","id":1016320,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2367_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2367\" data-vbnamecard=\"2367\">Resplendent Fire</a>, crap you're right! I completely forgot to elaborate on the Eugenic undertone. What I meant by that is that the Clans try to parody antiquated beliefs and concepts, like eugenics, to emphasize how removed from human society most elders of the Clans have become. However the inherent mechanics of the game itself accidentaly legitimize some of those belief by reinforcing them mechanically. This creates a subtext within the gameplay itself that subtly enforces such antiquated ideologies, like Eugenics. The biggest perpetrator of this is the Clan's insistence upon cultural history and customs to dictate Embraces, harkening back to the Eugenic belief of &quot;Good Breeding&quot; that was so popular with high society during the hight of imperialism. The Kindred would be discouraged from &quot;bringing undesirables into the family&quot; on pain of disownment or even Final Death if they did ever want to Embrace someone outside of their cultural or occupational circle. Thus the Clans remained &quot;pure&quot; and &quot;strong&quot; in the eyes of the elders, despite this concept being utter shit...except when we add Clan Disciplines into the mix. <br /> <br /> With the inclusion of the Clan Disciplines the subtext begins to undermine the original subversive purpose of the Elder's antiquated beliefs. Because, in Masquerade there are inherently more powerful Disciplines than others. And all of them are unique Clan Disciplines. To be more specific, I'll just use the most objectively powerful Discipline in the game as an example: Thaumaturgy. The Discipline of Thaunaturgy is, or was thanks to some damage control by Onyx Path, Clan Tremere's unique Discipline. And Clan Tremere's Embrace requisite, their &quot;good stock&quot; as it were, is for the candidate to be intelligent, comfortable in hierarchical organizations, have some knowledge or understanding of the occult, and be a throughow reasearcher with some experience with competitive academic environments (A.K.A. Academia.) Ergo, those Embraced into Clan Tremere are academics. Which means mechanically speaking, if you weren't an Academic then though luck. You'll never be accepted into Clan Tremere. Which meant tough luck, you'll never learn Thaumaturgy naturally. Which means tough luck, you'll always be inferior to a Tremere mechanically (And yes, with enough Celerity nothing else really matters. But this is about subtext. And the subtext is there.)<br /> <br /> This is the heart of the Eugenic subtext. It's why Clan Tremere is often either adored or reviled as the best or worst Clan. It makes it so that if you want to play a Tremere you have to play to their idea of &quot;good breeding&quot; if you want to get the most out of the Clan and benefit from the Clan Discipline to it's fullest. And people who don't want to play a &quot;ideal candidate&quot; get the shaft because the game makes Kindred Society so brutal when it comes to those who forsake tradition. And this is supposed to parody everything wrong with the Gentry, but instead it mechanically incentivizes romanticising the Peerage instead...*slowly looks directly into the camera with cold dead eyes*...which sucks because all they really need to do to fix this is either remove the Clan's Embrace prerequisites or make Thaumaturgy no longer a unique Discipline to the Tremere.<br /> <br /> Which the latter they did, because I think they realized too that unique Clan Disciplines set a dangerous subtext in a game about showcasing the worst of human societal norms and how they over time could lead to a world of pain, misery, despair, and darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 12-12-2016, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T17:12:28-08:00","id":1016323,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a> Thanks much! That clears it up for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013274-vampire-lite?p=1016319#post1016319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I was getting into this stuff in the 90s, the original World of Darkness attracted a lot of criticism for being &quot;politically correct.&quot; Goalposts shift.<br /> <br /> As it is, <i>Vampire </i>is not particularly polite, nor is it about people who do things correctly. It's about a glorious and unending cavalcade of big mistakes, made for both the best and worst of reasons. We should all be able to see ourselves making those mistakes... and so, <i>Vampire</i> includes diverse characters and viewpoints, in the hope that everyone can get in on the fun of feeling their lives going wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's like I keep saying, vampires ruin <i>everything</i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That's what I love about Vampire. One thing, at any rate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T17:22:55-08:00","id":1016329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013274-vampire-lite?p=1016239#post1016239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you guys are spending too much time thinking about race which leads to reading too deep into something that's not really there. According to modern pop culture: anything and everything is racist, which opens a new question of whether the current subject du jour is <i>actually</i> racist or just &amp;quot;racist&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's important to read deeply into media, so that we can recognize elements that perpetuate harmful ways of thinking, even when they aren't overt or intended. The media we consume affects the way we look at the world, and harmful attitudes are still harmful even if they aren't a result of willful and intentional malice. If we destingush between things that are &quot;<i>really</i> racist&quot; and things that are &quot;just 'racist'&quot;, we legitimize thought processes that lead to systemic power imbalance simply because they aren't overt or intentional. Because they're &quot;not <i>really</i> racist&quot;, that makes it ok.<br /> <br /> That's not to say that media should never feature anything problematic. It just means that we need to recognize the problematic aspects of our media and acknowledge them as being so, so as to not unintentionally legitimize them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T19:15:04-08:00","id":1016359,"title":"","content":"Without words to express how much I liked the thoughts constructed by both <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a> and @schizoPOP.<br /> <br /> Specially I found it true and clarifier the part on eugenics. Or, to be maybe better put, on how the game, by its mechanics and requisites, reinforced paradigms it was meant to criticize.<br /> <br /> A hell of a lot of players I know do this. Specially on Vampire and Werewolf. They mindlessly replicate the very concepts the game tries so hard to criticize. The problem of the game isn't the racist stereotypes existing. It is the game working in such a way that the players find it fitting to replicate what they &quot;should&quot; be striving to surpass.<br /> <br /> The game says that keeping Humanity is so hard, most vampires shrug it out or stop caring. It clearly wants the players to try hard, challenges them to keep Human. But the players mostly throw Humanity away and become monsters, because the game indeed makes high Humanity hard and unrewarding. Sometimes even uncool. The pattern repeats itself endlessly, with so much details.<br /> <br /> I remember a Werewolf game where the pack was every detail the assholes to Kinfolk, they did everything in the book. Uncaring rapist slaver monsters that sucked everything they could and just expecting that the Kinfolk were grateful for the opportunity to serve and striving to serve ever more, answering any slight with extreme violence. And they got sincerely surprised when the Kinfolk turned to their enemies. What was really sick about it is that the players went on to be &quot;Gaia's Sacred Warriors&quot;, and never actually perceived for a minute what they were doing. They just bought on the &quot;it must be done&quot; justification and thought themselves as pristine selfless heroes in the context of the game. The game meant to deliver a &quot;this is wrong, it is prejudice&quot; message, delivered instead the prejudice itself.<br /> <br /> Not that Masquerade is a bad game, it isn't. Nor is Apocalypse. But there are problems. And Requiem got rid of a lot of them. They aren't the same, and as much as Requiem isn't Vampire-Lite, it isn't Vampire-but-Better, either. It's just Other-Vampire. But it did corrected a lot of mistakes, or rather, avoided committing them. The saddest thing is that a lot of those problems can be solved in the Masquerade proper, but never was. I hope, though it is an admittedly weak hope, that they are addressed in the 5th edition.<br /> <br /> Just to showcase a little the point, let me take, instead of Thaumaturgy, Presence, and instead of Tremere, Toreador. You have a clan strongly linked to the arts, and you make a prejudicial view of said clan where it is considered vain, narcissistic and self-centered. Then you give said clan a Discipline that commands emotions, mostly to make people love you. And you finish by making it work mostly by using social rolls, but turning them to eleven in the most direct &quot;love me&quot; way. You finish by suggesting that Toreador dismiss or actively hate members who aren't on the arts. You make every tiny detail work to reinforce the very prejudice of the &quot;cynical and short-sighted&quot; society.<br /> <br /> Requiem did what? Since 1st edition Thaumaturgy was split in 3 different kinds of powers, each linked not to a family, but to a secret society that accepts believers as members. It was both made a lot less breaking and more interesting, and the game even went as far as to talk about Kindred with command of those powers who either got it by stealing or leaved the group, and it was consequential instead of &quot;daddy made a ritual and the Antitribu go boom&quot;. Or the less showy, but ever present clan blood hunt that was almost unavoidable in Masquerade, like how the Tremere hunted every Thaumaturgy user so thoroughly together with the traitorous teachers.<br /> <br /> Majesty on 2nd I simply fall in love. The Daeva, though with the same powers of the Brujah, was very much like the Toreador. That alone made a world of difference in 1st edition. But then I saw B&amp;S Majesty. A discipline that made the first dot from &quot;cool people are kings&quot; into &quot;anyone can be a king&quot;. That first dot alone was clever, simple, and made a world of difference both in rules and in setting. A Daeva can look every bit the Masquerade's Nosferatu, and yet command social situations with ease. The other levels built in to command emotions in a way far more complex and versatile, the Discipline was more awesome in every way and less &quot;vain&quot;, while still being as good for a character that wanted to be every bit the old Toreador.<br /> <br /> Finishing things, I'm sorry if some of it isn't very clear, I'm writing too much with only one good hand tonight, and something had to be left without add or correction. Yes, I write too much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T20:46:09-08:00","id":1016387,"title":"","content":"In my book, the most important thing in any RPG is the choices that player's make. Whether its choosing to kill an NPC or to buy that 4th dot of obfuscate, player agency is what defines the themes of the game. Both vampire gamelines tend to play the fascism card as part of the &quot;standard vampire court&quot; design. (Requiem 2e and Beckett's Jyhad Diary are bit more explicit that other systems do exist, but it's still a sort of assumed baseline for vampire politics.) Both of these games also give the player the ability to &quot;opt-out&quot; of the fascism by being Carthians or Anarchs. Bigoted NPCs can be shunned or thwarted.<br /> <br /> Removing those choices (or ignoring them from outset) is where things get uncomfortable for me. When an offensive concept shows up and the PCs are just expected to accept it and move on, the implication is that the aforementioned concept is somehow unimportant or &quot;no big deal.&quot; Requiem avoids it by having Clans be broad and subject to interpretation, and leaving just about everything else subject to player decisions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T09:23:18-08:00","id":1016592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013274-vampire-lite?p=1016359#post1016359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without words to express how much I liked the thoughts constructed by both <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3436_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3436\" data-vbnamecard=\"3436\">Dusksage</a> and @schizoPOP.<br /> <br /> Specially I found it true and clarifier the part on eugenics. Or, to be maybe better put, on how the game, by its mechanics and requisites, reinforced paradigms it was meant to criticize.<br /> <br /> A hell of a lot of players I know do this. Specially on Vampire and Werewolf. They mindlessly replicate the very concepts the game tries so hard to criticize. The problem of the game isn't the racist stereotypes existing. It is the game working in such a way that the players find it fitting to replicate what they &quot;should&quot; be striving to surpass.<br /> <br /> I remember a Werewolf game where the pack was every detail the assholes to Kinfolk, they did everything in the book. Uncaring rapist slaver monsters that sucked everything they could and just expecting that the Kinfolk were grateful for the opportunity to serve and striving to serve ever more, answering any slight with extreme violence. And they got sincerely surprised when the Kinfolk turned to their enemies. What was really sick about it is that the players went on to be &quot;Gaia's Sacred Warriors&quot;, and never actually perceived for a minute what they were doing. They just bought on the &quot;it must be done&quot; justification and thought themselves as pristine selfless heroes in the context of the game. The game meant to deliver a &quot;this is wrong, it is prejudice&quot; message, delivered instead the prejudice itself.<br /> <br /> Not that Masquerade is a bad game, it isn't. Nor is Apocalypse. But there are problems. And Requiem got rid of a lot of them. They aren't the same, and as much as Requiem isn't Vampire-Lite, it isn't Vampire-but-Better, either. It's just Other-Vampire. But it did corrected a lot of mistakes, or rather, avoided committing them. The saddest thing is that a lot of those problems can be solved in the Masquerade proper, but never was. I hope, though it is an admittedly weak hope, that they are addressed in the 5th edition.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I have had the opposite experience similarly, as you said to me the point of those game is to challenge stereotypes. And the games drive that point a lot of the time, anyone reading werewolf should be able to understand that the problem of Garou nation is that they eat up their own party line.<br /> <br /> My first Werewolf game i played a good silver fang, it was larp and chatting with the GM he told me that<br /> <br /> &quot;playing anti-stereotypes was dumb, and that &quot;true&quot; roleplayers play asshole Silver Fangs because everyone plays the non-racist Get of Feris, or the LGBT friendly Fianna or the good Silver Fang and that noone ever play the assholes because nobody wants to be the &quot;bad guy&quot; &quot;. I tried to explain that the game as presented *is* about playing the non-asshole garou and try to change the garou nation, thats the core message of the game, &quot;just because your endgoal is good doesnt absolve your asshole behavior&quot;<br /> <br /> I continue playing and then i was sudenly told that a) Reformist SF from revised werent a thing (which i wasnt told from when i made the PC and specifically mention then) and b) that my character was destined to be boring because &quot;All good Silver Fangs do is just making up bullshit reason why the tribe doesnt suck and then carry on&quot;<br /> <br /> And yet the game and i all was great, and most of the player really explore the ancient and inhuman society and it consecuences. I particularly remember a guy who played a fianna cub that went along to burn a building because a methlab was there and he went there wide eye ready to &quot;fight the wyrm and be part of the garou nation like a good little crusader&quot; and then another character intervene and explain to the rest of the cliaths and cub how that idea was moronic, short sighted an frankly prone to worsening the problem in more ways that solve it. With the fianna cub, just dropping his bat to the floor and walking away desilusioned of the whole garou nation and for the rest of the game the PC had a very humane look on the whole society.<br /> <br /> So i dont blame the game for that becuase if i, just reading the core, got the essence of the game in one read the fault is not really in the game but on bad players/DMs. The themes of brutal society, class, homophobia and racism should be there in those games because are part of the game and there is merit in exploring them. Removing then is not really solving them, because ignoring those themes is unrealistic to a degree. In both sense by either ignoring that racism and prejudice exist or by ignoring that is a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T10:10:56-08:00","id":1016621,"title":"","content":"Again, though, the game can recognize and acknowledge that those things are fucked up without having to remove them. If your game is about playing the bad guys, that's fine, as long as your game examines why what you're doing is bad. If it's just &quot;let's have fun pretending to be racist fucks with no consequences for a few hours&quot;, you're normalizing the behavior that you're imitating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T10:54:57-08:00","id":1016644,"title":"","content":"I think any Carthian would laugh at someone describing them as &quot;opting out of politics.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T11:02:06-08:00","id":1016649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013274-vampire-lite?p=1016621#post1016621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your game is about playing the bad guys, that's fine, as long as your game examines why what you're doing is bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's a lot more pushback against that idea than there once was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T12:50:26-08:00","id":1016689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013274-vampire-lite?p=1016592#post1016592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have had the opposite experience similarly, as you said to me the point of those game is to challenge stereotypes. And the games drive that point a lot of the time, anyone reading werewolf should be able to understand that the problem of Garou nation is that they eat up their own party line.<br /> <br /> My first Werewolf game i played a good silver fang, it was larp and chatting with the GM he told me that<br /> <br /> &quot;playing anti-stereotypes was dumb, and that &quot;true&quot; roleplayers play asshole Silver Fangs because everyone plays the non-racist Get of Feris, or the LGBT friendly Fianna or the good Silver Fang and that noone ever play the assholes because nobody wants to be the &quot;bad guy&quot; &quot;. I tried to explain that the game as presented *is* about playing the non-asshole garou and try to change the garou nation, thats the core message of the game, &quot;just because your endgoal is good doesnt absolve your asshole behavior&quot;<br /> <br /> I continue playing and then i was sudenly told that a) Reformist SF from revised werent a thing (which i wasnt told from when i made the PC and specifically mention then) and b) that my character was destined to be boring because &quot;All good Silver Fangs do is just making up bullshit reason why the tribe doesnt suck and then carry on&quot;<br /> <br /> And yet the game and i all was great, and most of the player really explore the ancient and inhuman society and it consecuences. I particularly remember a guy who played a fianna cub that went along to burn a building because a methlab was there and he went there wide eye ready to &quot;fight the wyrm and be part of the garou nation like a good little crusader&quot; and then another character intervene and explain to the rest of the cliaths and cub how that idea was moronic, short sighted an frankly prone to worsening the problem in more ways that solve it. With the fianna cub, just dropping his bat to the floor and walking away desilusioned of the whole garou nation and for the rest of the game the PC had a very humane look on the whole society.<br /> <br /> So i dont blame the game for that becuase if i, just reading the core, got the essence of the game in one read the fault is not really in the game but on bad players/DMs. The themes of brutal society, class, homophobia and racism should be there in those games because are part of the game and there is merit in exploring them. Removing then is not really solving them, because ignoring those themes is unrealistic to a degree. In both sense by either ignoring that racism and prejudice exist or by ignoring that is a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>1- I never said the game didn't proposed that. On the contrary, and as you say, it is pretty clear in the book.<br /> <br /> 2- I did said that details abundant on the game encouraged players to embrace the stereotypes by how they make the game work. It wasn't, though, the game's intent.<br /> <br /> 3- Never said it was unavoidable. I personally always liked to play nice, or to play bad and find redemption and drama. The character I liked the most to play, and more successful one, was nice.<br /> <br /> 4- I abhor the notion of player or ST being bad for not &quot;getting the essence of the game&quot;. If it happened once or twice, I would call it a quirk of the group. It happens frequently, so the fault is in the game, and in the game alone, for not giving the tool to adequately demonstrates what is on the fluff.<br /> <br /> 5- I said CoD removed problems, not themes. All of those themes are there all the same. The difference is that the game actually lets you demonstrate the other side. And yes, the themes in fact aren't hammered in the game, so people who don't want to play out those themes don't have to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T17:40:07-08:00","id":1016835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013274-vampire-lite?p=1016644#post1016644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think any Carthian would laugh at someone describing them as &quot;opting out of politics.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Politics is mugging by other means.&quot;<br /> --Comrade Princess, Los Angeles Movement","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T18:12:24-08:00","id":1016846,"title":"","content":"At the end of the day, when it comes to themes, set up expectations first. Storytellers should lay out what themes and topics could or will come up in the chronicle, and things they won't allow. Players should bring up anything they are uncomfortable with, so that the Storyteller can avoid those subjects or present them in ways that aren't going to cross a line. Honestly, communication is key.<br /> <br /> As far as themes go, I think the important thing is that things like Integrity and Humanity probably exist on something like a bell curve: a handful of saints and monsters, and most people sitting right in the middle, most people being kind of okay or kind of jerks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T06:17:29-08:00","id":1017021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013274-vampire-lite?p=1016835#post1016835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Politics is mugging by other means.&quot;<br /> --Comrade Princess, Los Angeles Movement</div> </div> </div> </div>And then, NYC sent a brute squad to LA to kidnap Princess and &quot;bring her into the fold.&quot; <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T10:06:42-08:00","id":1017126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1013274-vampire-lite?p=1016621#post1016621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, though, the game can recognize and acknowledge that those things are fucked up without having to remove them. If your game is about playing the bad guys, that's fine, as long as your game examines why what you're doing is bad. If it's just &quot;let's have fun pretending to be racist fucks with no consequences for a few hours&quot;, you're normalizing the behavior that you're imitating.</div> </div> </div> </div>After the last few threads on this topic in the Masquerade thread, it typically feels like more people argue including those explicit themes as validation more than anything. I don't think anyone has ever said racism, sexism, homophobia don't exist in cWoD. But somehow it is a problem for them if it isn't spelled out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T13:29:14-08:00","id":1017267,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12552_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12552\" data-vbnamecard=\"12552\">Monalfie</a> I think that's more a reaction to people not wanting to see it at all. Or you get people saying they're reading too much into the games if they see it in the games.<br /> <br /> Plus there's more than one way to incorporate such themes into a game. One way does so as a way to reinforce those things, which can exclude. Another way does so as a way to highlight those things without excluding.<br /> <br /> It's not so much that it needs to be spelled out, but rather that it needs to be handled with some sensitivity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T12:38:16-08:00","id":1025529,"title":"","content":"Meh, I always preferred 1e Requiem's &quot;Masquerade Lite&quot; approach to the metaplot-heavy madness of Masquerade or the approach 2e Requiem took. It's a well known fact around here that I am not a fan of 2e Requiem so I won't go on about that too much, but I love 1e Requiem (with some hacks, of course), and I never understood why people think that being &quot;Masquerade Lite&quot; is a bad thing.<br /> <br /> \u200bTo me, 1e Requiem kept the best parts of Masquerade and dropped a lot of the bad parts such as the metaplot, the cultural stereotyping, and a lot of other baggage. I think 2e tried to reinvent the wheel too hard and had issues of its own, but other people like 2e and that is fine with me. So, yeah, I kind of like the &quot;Masquerade Lite&quot; approach that Requiem initially took, never cared for the themes of personal horror, but as an ST, that can be amended easily via Rule Zero. Otherwise, Requiem is an awesome game. Masquerade is decent too, but Requiem is excellent for an entirely different yet similar reason.<br /> <br /> \u200bI never liked the hardcore Masquerade fans who won't take off their rose-tinted nostalgia goggles long enough to give Requiem a proper chance. Maybe it's because they dominate the WoD fandom and LARP scene in Roanoke, Virginia, but either way, nostalgia isn't what it used to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}